    <item>
      <title>Legally Validated Evaluation Framework for Voice Anonymization</title>
      <link>https://brijmohan.github.io/publication/eval-framework-is25/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 17 Aug 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://brijmohan.github.io/publication/eval-framework-is25/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code.&lt;/strong&gt; The reference implementation of both metrics is open source as &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/brijmohan/voice-anonymization-legal-eval&#34;&gt;voice-anonymization-legal-eval&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;code&gt;pip install voice-anonymization-legal-eval&lt;/code&gt;), with the score matrices and dataset definitions on &lt;a href=&#34;https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23142030&#34;&gt;Zenodo&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On the CNIL&amp;rsquo;s role, stated precisely.&lt;/strong&gt; In August 2024 the Technological Expertise Department of the CNIL, the French data protection authority, reviewed Nijta&amp;rsquo;s Voice Harbor solution and identified no obstacle to it demonstrating compliance with the three anonymization criteria of Article 29 Working Party Opinion 05/2014. These metrics were the vehicle of that demonstration. It is a technical opinion on a solution, not a certification of the metrics, and it does not transfer to an organisation deploying the solution, which must demonstrate anonymity in its own context.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
    </item>
    
